  Permanent gaps (present at both n=5 and n=6): Δ=[3], H=[7]


PART 10: WHERE DO 7, 13, 19 APPEAR IN TOURNAMENT DATA?
------------------------------------------------------------

  7 as FORBIDDEN:
    H = 7 impossible for all n
    α₁ = 3 with α₂ = 0 impossible (triangle overshoot)
    Binary: Δ = 3 = 011 gap

  13 as SURPRISE:
    H = 13 achievable at n=5: 120 tournaments
    Δ = 6 = 110 (binary): α₁ even, α₂ odd (2 independent pairs)

  19 as OCR FACTOR:
    133 = 7 × 19 = Var(H) denominator at n=5
    19 ≡ 1 (mod 6): compatible with hexagonal (3-fold) symmetry
    19 = 20 - 1 = 4×5 - 1

  INTERMEDIATE PRODUCTS:
    7 × 13 = 91 = 10² - 9 = C(5,2)² - 3²
    7 × 19 = 133 = OCR denominator at n=5
    13 × 19 = 247 = 13 × 19
    91 = nonzero Walsh coefficients at n=5 (from S112)


